        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Delegated User Authorization (OAuth Token Exchange)]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[Exchanges the user's token and the agent's own identity for a short-lived, single-audience, minimally scoped token immediately before each tool call, so that the agent acts with delegated and attributable authority instead of a shared super-credential]]></description>
            <link>https://agentic-patterns.com/patterns/delegated-user-auth-token-exchange</link>
            <guid isPermaLink="true">https://agentic-patterns.com/patterns/delegated-user-auth-token-exchange</guid>
            <category><![CDATA[Security & Safety]]></category>
            <category><![CDATA[oauth]]></category>
            <category><![CDATA[token-exchange]]></category>
            <category><![CDATA[delegation]]></category>
            <category><![CDATA[least-privilege]]></category>
            <category><![CDATA[on-behalf-of]]></category>
            <category><![CDATA[audit-attribution]]></category>
            <category><![CDATA[multi-tenant]]></category>
            <category><![CDATA[identity]]></category>
            <pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Dual LLM Pattern]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[Splits work between a privileged LLM that calls tools but never sees untrusted data and a quarantined LLM that reads untrusted data but has no tools]]></description>
            <link>https://agentic-patterns.com/patterns/dual-llm-pattern</link>
            <guid isPermaLink="true">https://agentic-patterns.com/patterns/dual-llm-pattern</guid>
            <category><![CDATA[Orchestration & Control]]></category>
            <category><![CDATA[privilege-separation]]></category>
            <category><![CDATA[quarantined-llm]]></category>
            <category><![CDATA[symbolic-variables]]></category>
            <pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Dual-Speed Realtime Architecture (Talker-Reasoner)]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[Splits an agent into a fast Talker that owns the live conversation and a slow Reasoner that plans and calls tools in the background, with a shared belief state as their only coupling, so that the user gets a reply at once while the deep work runs]]></description>
            <link>https://agentic-patterns.com/patterns/dual-speed-talker-reasoner-architecture</link>
            <guid isPermaLink="true">https://agentic-patterns.com/patterns/dual-speed-talker-reasoner-architecture</guid>
            <category><![CDATA[Orchestration & Control]]></category>
            <category><![CDATA[talker-reasoner]]></category>
            <category><![CDATA[dual-process]]></category>
            <category><![CDATA[realtime]]></category>
            <category><![CDATA[background-reasoning]]></category>
            <category><![CDATA[shared-belief-state]]></category>
            <category><![CDATA[latency]]></category>
            <category><![CDATA[asynchronous-agents]]></category>
            <pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Durable Execution & Step Checkpointing]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[Replays a durable step history to resume crashed, rate-limited, or approval-paused agent runs from the last completed step, without repeating finished LLM calls or committed side effects]]></description>
            <link>https://agentic-patterns.com/patterns/durable-execution-step-checkpointing</link>
            <guid isPermaLink="true">https://agentic-patterns.com/patterns/durable-execution-step-checkpointing</guid>
